yrewrite_htaccess_info = To use YRewrite, a .htaccess file is created in the root folder. If another .htaccess file already exists, it will be replaced. Please back up the .htaccess file beforehand if necessary.

yrewrite_info_headline = Using YRewrite
yrewrite_info_text = Since YRewrite is intended for <mark>multidomain setups</mark>, there are certain prerequisites. All URL replacements are handled by YRewrite. This means a URL may contain the domain name depending on the situation. Therefore please <mark>do not use a base tag</mark> in templates. If something gets mixed up due to custom development or similar, please clear the general cache. This allows YRewrite to recreate the config and URL files.
yrewrite_info_tipps = Tips
yrewrite_info_tipps_text = <ul><li>All <mark>settings under <i>System</i></mark> (website URL, start article and error article) are <mark>ignored</mark> when using YRewrite.</li><li>If <mark>only one domain</mark> is used, the field <code>Mount point of the domain</code> in the domain settings must be left empty.</li></ul>
yrewrite_info_seo = Using the SEO options
yrewrite_info_seo_text = Please put the following code <mark>into the template</mark> in the <mark>&lt;head&gt;</mark> section. Do not use your own title and description tags.
yrewrite_info_sitemaprobots = sitemap.xml and robots.txt

